# AI-Agent-Talkshow — project rules

## Language

- **All git-tracked files must be in English** (README, ROADMAP, CONTRIBUTING, YAML comments, new code comments).
- Do not add Chinese to files that will be pushed to GitHub.
- `.cursor/session-memory.md`, `skill.md`, `soul.md`, `avatar-plan.md`, `av-sync-progress.md` are local notes (gitignored except rules in `.cursor/rules/` and skills in `.cursor/skills/`).

## Before coding

1. Read `.cursor/session-memory.md` for current sprint.
2. Read [ROADMAP.md](../../ROADMAP.md) for priorities.
3. Read [.cursor/skills/ai-agent-talkshow/SKILL.md](../skills/ai-agent-talkshow/SKILL.md) for durable domain knowledge (floor control, key paths, deploy).
4. For avatar/UI work: read `.cursor/avatar-plan.md`.
5. For transcript/lip-sync timing: read `.cursor/av-sync-progress.md`.
6. Read [README.md](../../README.md) for setup and architecture.

## Architecture constraints

- **Single LiveKit agent participant** with role handoff — do not spawn 3 separate RTC agents without explicit design approval.
- **Shared `show_history`** — panelists share one transcript; disambiguate roles in prompts (Human guest ≠ Amy).
- **Gemma calls:** `complete_from_wav` (human audio) and `complete_text` (panel lines); `StoredReplyLLM` does not call the model again.
- **Floor control:** strict FIFO hand-raise queue; poll batch tie-break via `panel_priority` (one AI winner per poll); skip poll/open floor when queue non-empty; after human turn always open floor + poll when queue empty (see `agent/floor/floor_control.py` `after_human_turn`, `agent/floor/host_floor.py`).

